Captions in list items do not create a paragraph gap

```
- | a |
  ^ cap
- c
.
<ul>
  <li>
    <table>
      <caption>cap</caption>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>a</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </li>
  <li>c</li>
</ul>
```

```
- | a |

  ^ cap
- c
.
<ul>
  <li>
    <table>
      <caption>cap</caption>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>a</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </li>
  <li>c</li>
</ul>
```

```
- | a |


  ^ cap
- c
.
<ul>
  <li>
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>a</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>^ cap</p>
  </li>
  <li><p>c</p></li>
</ul>
```

```
- ![a](b.png)

  ^ cap
- c
.
<ul>
  <li>
    <figure>
      <img src="b.png" alt="a">
      <figcaption>cap</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </li>
  <li>c</li>
</ul>
```

```
- > q

  ^ cap
- c
.
<ul>
  <li>
    <figure>
      <blockquote><p>q</p></blockquote>
      <figcaption>cap</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </li>
  <li>c</li>
</ul>
```

````
- ```
  x
  ```

  ^ cap
- c
.
<ul>
  <li>
    <figure>
      <pre><code>x
</code></pre>
      <figcaption>cap</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </li>
  <li>c</li>
</ul>
````

```
- $$`x`

  ^ cap
- c
.
<ul>
  <li>
    <figure>
      <p><span class="math display" role="math">\[x\]</span></p>
      <figcaption>cap</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </li>
  <li>c</li>
</ul>
```

